{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.436, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 24, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.001Z", "t_ms": 7288, "delta": "Yes, running agents on AIOS maintains and, in several cases, improves their benchmark performance"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.49, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 25, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.153Z", "t_ms": 7439, "delta": " [C2]. \n\nEvaluations across four standard benchmarks (HumanEval, MINT code subset, GAIA, and"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.674, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 26, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.336Z", "t_ms": 7622, "delta": " SWE-Bench-Lite) using GPT-4o-mini show that AIOS consistently maintains success rates and can boost performance through"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.847, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.510Z", "t_ms": 7797, "delta": " specific kernel mechanisms [C2]:\n\n* **Code Generation Benchmarks (HumanEval, MINT, SWE-Bench-Lite):**"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.023, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.683Z", "t_ms": 7969, "delta": " AIOS boosts agent performance via prompt enhancement inside the LLM wrapper, which embeds system prompts with more structural inputs and outputs to provide additional"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.172, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:43.836Z", "t_ms": 8122, "delta": " context and guidance [C2].\n* **Tool-Calling Benchmarks (GAIA):** Agent performance is boosted through"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.438, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:44.099Z", "t_ms": 8386, "delta": " two mechanisms: pre-execution parameter validation using structural regex to verify tool-call formatting prior to execution, and conflict resolution has"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.57, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:44.232Z", "t_ms": 8519, "delta": "hmaps to resolve concurrent access issues [C2].\n\nFurthermore, evaluating the context switch mechanism with Mistral-7B and L"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.854, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:44.518Z", "t_ms": 8804, "delta": "lama-3-8B yielded BLEU and BERT similarity scores of 1.0 between outputs generated with context switching"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.039, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:44.703Z", "t_ms": 8989, "delta": " enabled versus disabled, confirming that switching contexts introduces no discrepancies in output quality [C3]. In addition to maintaining or improving accuracy"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.238, "data": {"request_id": "ff6f9917480c", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:13:44.902Z", "t_ms": 9189, "delta": ", AIOS achieves up to $2.1\\times$ faster execution speeds for serving agents [C1]."}}
